but that's where that requirement comes in Otherwise when it comes to just owner petitioned annexations it just says it needs to be contiguous Um so that that's what's in state statute and I believe Mr Lloyd might come and correct me if I'm wrong or provide more information Mr Lloyd Madam Chair if I may Seth Lloyd with the city of Shine Planning and Development Department Um there are four different ways to add land to the city and state statute One of them is an addition by Platt I have never done that in my time here so I don't exactly know the process on that one very clearly Um another is when the city initiates an annexation of city- owned land Means the city is the sole owner city is the sole initiator Um

that's a different process A third is when the city initiates annexation of land it does not own Um that's where the 75% contiguous comes in Um the 75% is only where um people being annexed cannot protest So the city can actually initiate an annexation where the land is only say 10% contiguous But at that point if people pro enough people protests that annexation be stopped Um and then the fourth is by landowner petition The landowner petition annexation process only requires a majority of the land owners to petition It does not require 100% of land owners And also that exempts any taxexempt entity from that requirement So if there was um a land owner who if there were three land owners and

they requested to annex a church and uh two other properties that didn't sign on the church as a taxexempt property would not count against that majority and then three owners versus two owners the three owners would be over the two owners So um because this is a landowner annexation and because the city is taxexempt um that can be added without the city officially signing any petition to annex I hope that clarifies all of those elements of statute and annexations There's certainly a lot more I could delve into This is men chairman uh chairwoman throughu Could you explain the city's land that we're the city is trying to annex um I I always understood that city- owned property regardless of where whether it was contiguous or not could be annexed Uh

